        <tr> 
          <td height="622"> 
            <div align="justify"> 
              <table width="90%" height="587" border="1" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#3B6692">
                <tr> 
                  <td height="585"> 
                    <div align="justify"></div>
                    <div align="justify"></div>
                    <div align="justify"> 
                      <table width="90%" height="535" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                        <tr> 
                          <td width="30%" height="143"><img src="/datacenter/util/imgs/mn_menu_11_en.jpg" width="152" height="178"></td>
                          <td width="3%" height="143"></td>
                          <td width="67%" height="143"><div align="justify"> <font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">This 
                              item allows users to input, edit and delete vehicle 
                              data similar to the item Drivers &gt; Management.</font><br>
                            </div></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr> 
                          <td height="357" colspan="3"> 
                            <ul>
                              <li> 
                                <div align="justify"><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">	
                                  To <strong>Add</strong> a vehicle click on &#8216;&#8220;Add 
                                  Vehicle&#8221;. All the fields marked with * 
                                  must be filled in. The input will be sent to 
                                  supervision and the CEPA team will be in charge 
                                  of making the any corrections and requesting 
                                  further information as necessary.</font></div>
                              </li>
                            </ul>
                            <ul>
                              <li> <font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                                To <strong>Delete</strong> a vehicle users must 
                                first perform a simple or advanced search, establishing 
                                the selected criteria. A drop-down list containing 
                                all the vehicles that meet the selected criteria 
                                will appear. The user should then select the vehicle 
                                to be deleted and click &#8220;Inactive&#8221; 
                                on the next screen. Fill in the &#8220;exclusion 
                                date&#8221; and &#8220;comments&#8221; (reason 
                                for the deletion) and click on the &#8220;Inactivate&#8221; 
                                button. This vehicle will no longer be active 
                                (available) for queries or searches, however the 
                                recorded data (mileage, events, etc.) will not 
                                be deleted. </font> </li>
                            </ul>
                            <div align="justify"> 
                              <ul>
                                <li><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                                  To <strong>Edit</strong> a vehicle users must 
                                  first perform a search where the characteristics 
                                  of the vehicle will be established. This search 
                                  will display a list of vehicles that meet the 
                                  selected criteria.<br>
                                  Click on the license plate of the vehicle, then 
                                  click &#8220;Edit&#8221; on the next screen, 
                                  inform the necessary changes and click on &#8220;Save&#8221;.</font></li>
                              </ul>
                            </div>
                            <ul type="square">
                            </ul></td>
